{"id":"10-11.FirstCar","contentHtml":"<p>This is the starting point of my entire journey. The year is 2010, I am 12 years old. A computer at that time was almost a luxury for me.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The desire to create games was stronger than the circumstances.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>The main challenge was <strong>overcoming the almost complete lack of resources</strong>: I didn't have my own computer, and access to one was limited to a few hours on weekends. The task was to find a way to learn and practice under such conditions.</p>\n<h2>Solution</h2>\n<p>I developed my own <strong>\"offline learning system\"</strong>: I downloaded video tutorials for the good old <code>Construct Classic</code>, burned them onto CDs, and at home, during the week, <strong>studied them on a DVD player</strong>.</p>\n<p>Theory was studied without a computer, and on weekends I traveled to the other side of the city to apply the accumulated knowledge in practice.</p>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>First Completed Game:</strong> Despite all the difficulties, I created my first finished project — a top-down 2D maze with graphics, win/loss logic, <mark>where you have to control a car without hitting the walls</mark>.</li>\n<li><strong>Defining the Vocation:</strong> Although the source code hasn't survived, this experience was decisive. <mark>It was at that moment I realized that creating games is my life's work</mark>. This project is not about technology, but about the birth of the passion that drives me to this day.</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"First Game: Maze on Construct Classic","date":"2010-11","type":"project","tagsArray":["PC","Construct Classic"],"heroVideo":null,"shortDescription":"<p>Created my first 2D game at 12, learning the engine from tutorials watched on a <strong>DVD player</strong>.</p>\n","projectIcon":"/images/projects/10-11.FirstCar/icon.webp","screenshots":[]}